[00:25.07] It is early yet, my love
[00:28.21] You've scarcely begun to know life
[00:34.08] And already you speak of taking your leave
[00:39.56] Not even knowing which way you will go
[00:45.37] 
[00:48.22] Take heed, my dear
[00:52.03] Though I know your mind is made up
[00:57.51] At every corner, a little of your life falls away
[01:03.27] Before long, you will no longer be who you are
[01:08.48] 
[01:10.99] Hear me well, my love
[01:14.60] Take heed: the world is a mill
[01:20.50] It will grind your dreams away, so heartless
[01:26.32] It will reduce your illusions to dust
[01:30.86] 
[01:33.73] Take heed, my dear
[01:37.48] From every love, you'll inherit nothing but cynicism
[01:42.95] By the time you see it, you'll be at the brink
[01:48.94] Of the abyss you dug with your own feet
